<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24478" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interstĭtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		intersisto. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A pause</i>, <i>respite</i>, <i>interval</i>, Gell. praef. <i>init.</i>; <i><span class="en">id. 20, 1, 43</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A difference</i>, <i>distinction</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interstitio fieri quae poterit singulorum, cum,
					qui Juppiter fuerat, idem possit existimari Mars esse?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 6, 198</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
